# Per-scope MEMORY PACKET caps in bytes. Copy to packet-limits.conf to use.
# Format: scope<TAB>bytes  (or scope=bytes). Lines starting with # are ignored.
# Scopes absent from this file keep the built-in default (14000 bytes ~= 3.5k
# tokens per injection). Floor: 4000 -- smaller values are clamped.
#
# When to raise a cap: spine-health reports packet starvation for a scope
# (small coverage share AND a small absolute window). One oversized scope gets
# breathing room here WITHOUT taxing the injection cost of every other scope.
# Non-ASCII vaults hit caps sooner: UTF-8 spends 2+ bytes per character.
#
# my-biggest-scope	20000
